{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/492019-on-the-harvest-merit-and-gambling-through-the-wyrd","id":492019,"title":"On The Harvest Merit And Gambling Through The Wyrd","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-25T15:23:28-07:00","id":492019,"title":"On The Harvest Merit And Gambling Through The Wyrd","content":"How do you interpret/use the Harvest Merit? I do it like this:<br /> <br /> When you purchase dots in a Harvesting source, you have 1 &quot;floating&quot; point of Glamour for each dot in the type of Harvest. These floating points of Glamour represent run-of-the-mill Harvesting done in downtime: pledges, emotions, dreams and goblin fruit. These stored points are refreshed each chapter (game session) and may be accessed at any time, but the more dots in Harvest you have, the busier you are. Assume that, during each story, for each type of Harvesting you have at 3 dots or more, you must &quot;sow&quot; glamour for that type to guarantee a full Harvest.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> Fulfilling important mission-Pledges for the Seasonal King/Queen or serving the Freehold in a significant way.<br /> <br /> Causing an interesting instance of an emotion in someone (passively absorbing glamour doesn't count). Summer = challenge someone to prove they are as skilled as they say, ideally by pitting themselves against you and having a good duel. Winter = show or remind them of painful truths, ideally to make them more mature. Spring = contribute to making their greatest desires come true, ideally more productive than hedonistic escapades. Autumn = prevent someone from delving further into a situation, ideally to protect important secrets.<br /> <br /> Creating a dreamscape representing one or more of your most significant conflicts, and then devouring it. Devouring a dreamscape simply requires you to resolve the dream conflict, ideally as practice for facing the real deal.<br /> <br /> Growing and taking care of your own goblin fruit garden. This requires you to go out into the Hedge and gather food for your plants, which might require a trip to a goblin market or catching some hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> Also, what if there were Freeholds/Hedge Towns/Skein Threads where changelings could win glamour by gambling through the Wyrd, using Tokens as a kind of poker chips? To participate in Wyrd Gambling, you essentially sign a quick Contract with the concept of Chance with the Wyrd acting as the middle man, like with most fae magic. You determine the level of the bet by writing down what you think will happen and the name of the Tokens you are wagering, then signing with your moniker. These Wyrd Casinos have built-in goblin markets where you may buy Tokens/Wyrd chips to bet. The risks and potential rewards are proportional to the total dot rating of the Tokens you wager. If you win, your Tokens go to the owner of the Wyrd Casino, but you receive glamour points equal to [total dots of the Tokens x 15]. These glamour points are stored in a separate pool with no upper limit, which you may use to buy expensive items on goblin markets, or activate special Contracts at the ST's discretion. If you lose, your Tokens go to the owner of the Wyrd Casino, and depending on the game, you receive less glamour than you could have received or no glamour at all..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-25-2015, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:",